@startuml
title Better Auth + Supabase RLS bridge - UI + auth + API request sequence
autonumber

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontColor #202124
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #2F5D8A
  LifeLineBorderColor #8A8A8A
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  ParticipantBorderColor #2F5D8A
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF2FA
  ParticipantFontColor #202124
  ActorBorderColor #2F5D8A
  ActorBackgroundColor #EAF2FA
  ActorFontColor #202124
  GroupBorderColor #8A8A8A
  GroupBackgroundColor #F7F7F7
  GroupFontColor #202124
}

actor Client

box "Cloudflare edge: single deployed Worker service (items-api-worker)" #EAF2FA
participant "Worker entrypoint\nrouter + /items handlers" as Worker
participant "Better Auth module\n(in-process library)" as BetterAuth
participant "JWT bridge module\n(in-process library)" as Bridge
database "Worker Secret\nES256 private JWK" as WorkerKey
end box

participant "Cloudflare Hyperdrive\nSUPABASE_HYPERDRIVE" as Hyperdrive
collections "Worker Static Assets\nASSETS (ui/dist)" as Assets

box "Supabase platform" #E8F5E9
participant "Supabase Data API\n(PostgREST)" as DataAPI
collections "Supabase public\nJWT signing key" as SupabaseKeys
database "Postgres auth tables\nuser/session/account/verification/rate_limit" as AuthDB
database "Postgres app tables\nitems + RLS policies" as AppDB
end box

note over Worker,BetterAuth
Same deployment unit.
No network hop between Worker and Better Auth.
These are in-process function calls.
end note

== Responsibilities ==
note over BetterAuth
AuthN and session responsibility:
- /api/auth/* endpoints
- bearer session token issue and verify
- user/session/account persistence
end note

note over Worker,Bridge
Application API responsibility:
- /items CRUD orchestration
- mint short-lived Supabase JWT
- call Supabase Data API
end note

note over DataAPI,AppDB
Supabase responsibility:
- verify Worker-signed JWT
- enforce auth.uid() RLS on app tables
end note

== UI request ==
Client -> Worker: GET / (Accept: text/html)
Worker --> Client: 302 redirect to /ui
Client -> Worker: GET /ui
Worker -> Assets: env.ASSETS.fetch(/index.html)
Assets --> Worker: HTML response
Worker --> Client: UI response

== Sign-in / sign-up ==
Client -> Worker: POST /api/auth/sign-up/email or /api/auth/sign-in/email
Worker -> BetterAuth: in-process auth.handler(request)
BetterAuth -> Hyperdrive: query/insert auth records
Hyperdrive -> AuthDB: SQL read/write
AuthDB --> Hyperdrive: auth rows
Hyperdrive --> BetterAuth: persistence result
BetterAuth --> Worker: auth response + set-auth-token header
Worker --> Client: auth payload + set-auth-token

== Protected API call ==
Client -> Worker: GET|POST|PATCH|DELETE / with Authorization: Bearer token
Worker -> BetterAuth: in-process getSession(headers, request)
BetterAuth -> Hyperdrive: read session + user
Hyperdrive -> AuthDB: SELECT session and user
AuthDB --> Hyperdrive: session + user
Hyperdrive --> BetterAuth: session payload

alt Missing or invalid session
  BetterAuth --> Worker: null or invalid session
  Worker --> Client: 401 Authentication is required
else Valid session
  BetterAuth --> Worker: session.user.id + email
  Worker -> Bridge: in-process mint bridge JWT (TTL 300s)
  Bridge -> WorkerKey: load ES256 private JWK
  Bridge --> Worker: signed JWT (sub=user.id, role=authenticated)
  note right of Worker
  Claims used for Supabase Data API:
  sub = Better Auth user.id
  role = authenticated
  email = session user email
  end note
  Worker -> DataAPI: CRUD request with Authorization: Bearer bridge JWT
  DataAPI -> SupabaseKeys: verify ES256 signature + kid
  SupabaseKeys --> DataAPI: token trusted
  DataAPI -> AppDB: execute query as authenticated
  AppDB -> AppDB: auth.uid() = JWT sub\nRLS checks items.user_id ownership

  alt RLS allows
    AppDB --> DataAPI: rows / mutation result
    DataAPI --> Worker: success payload
    Worker --> Client: success payload
  else RLS denies
    AppDB --> DataAPI: denied / empty result
    DataAPI --> Worker: denied response
    Worker --> Client: error or empty payload
  end
end

@enduml
